IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era25-types`

-- Employment Rights Act 2025 (UK) — GOALS 1-3: STATUTORY SICK PAY, THE
-- UNFAIR DISMISSAL QUALIFYING PERIOD, AND GUARANTEED-HOURS COMPLAINT TIME
-- LIMITS.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2025-36.txt.

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

§ `Goal 1 — statutory sick pay`

-- SSCBA s 157(1) as substituted by s 11(2): "The weekly rate of statutory
-- sick pay that an employer must pay to an employee is the lower of— (a)
-- £118.75, and (b) 80% of the employee's normal weekly earnings." s 11(3):
-- the lower earnings limit exclusion is omitted.
@ref s 11 (SSCBA s 157(1), Sch 11 para 2)
@export The weekly rate of statutory sick pay under s 157(1) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 as substituted by s 11 of the Employment Rights Act 2025 (UK): the lower of £118.75 and 80% of normal weekly earnings, with no lower earnings limit. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Sickness facts`  @desc The employee's normal weekly earnings
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` s MEANS
    IF eighty AT MOST 118.75 THEN eighty ELSE 118.75
    WHERE
        eighty MEANS s's `normal weekly earnings` TIMES 0.8

-- SSCBA s 152(2) as amended by s 10(3): a period of incapacity is "a period
-- of one day which is, or of two or more consecutive days each of which is,"
-- a day of incapacity; s 155(1) (the three waiting days) is omitted; s 153(1)
-- the period of entitlement begins with the "first" day.
@ref s 10 (SSCBA ss 152(2), 153(1), 155)
@export The first day for which statutory sick pay is payable under the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 as amended by s 10 of the Employment Rights Act 2025 (UK): the first day of incapacity, with no waiting days (any period of one or more days of incapacity counts). NOTHING if there is no day of incapacity. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Sickness facts`  @desc The first day and number of days of incapacity
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the first day statutory sick pay is payable for` s MEANS
    IF s's `days of incapacity` AT LEAST 1 THEN JUST (s's `first day of incapacity`) ELSE NOTHING

§ `Goal 2 — the unfair dismissal qualifying period`

-- ERA 1996 s 108(1) as amended by s 25(2): "unless he has been continuously
-- employed for a period of not less than six months ending with the
-- effective date of termination". (2): one month for a s 64(2) dismissal;
-- (3)-(5): no period for the listed reasons. s 25(3): s 124 (the cap) is
-- omitted.
@ref s 25 (ERA 1996 s 108)
@export Whether the qualifying period for unfair dismissal in s 108 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, as amended by s 25 of the Employment Rights Act 2025 (UK), is met: continuous employment of six months ending with the effective date of termination; one month for a s 64(2) dismissal; none where s 108(3)-(5) applies. (The compensatory award is no longer capped: s 124 is omitted.) DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A `Dismissal facts`  @desc The start of continuous employment, the effective date of termination, and the s 64(2) and s 108(3)-(5) facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the six-month qualifying period is met in` d IF
    BRANCH
        IF d's `a reason needing no qualifying period` THEN TRUE
        IF d's `dismissed for a s 64(2) requirement` THEN
            d's `effective date of termination` AT LEAST `the last day of the` 1 `months beginning with` (d's `continuous employment began on`)
        OTHERWISE
            d's `effective date of termination` AT LEAST `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` (d's `continuous employment began on`)

§ `Goal 3 — guaranteed-hours complaint time limits`

-- ERA 1996 s 207B(3): days from the day after Day A to Day B, so far as
-- within the period, are not counted; (4): if the limit would expire between
-- Day A and one month after Day B, it expires then.
@ref ERA 1996 s 207B(3)-(4)
GIVEN limit IS A DATE, start IS A DATE, e IS AN `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the limit` limit `of a period from` start `extended by` e MEANS
    IF       afterThree AT LEAST e's `Day A`
         AND afterThree AT MOST oneMonthAfterB
    THEN oneMonthAfterB
    ELSE afterThree
    WHERE
        first MEANS `the later of` (Date (Day (e's `Day A`) PLUS 1)) start
        stopped MEANS Day (e's `Day B`) MINUS Day first PLUS 1
        afterThree MEANS
            IF   e's `Day A` LESS THAN limit AND stopped GREATER THAN 0
            THEN Date (Day limit PLUS stopped)
            ELSE limit
        oneMonthAfterB MEANS `add months` (e's `Day B`) 1

-- s 27BH(1)-(7): "before the end of the period of six months beginning with
-- the day after" the trigger; (8): "beginning with the day on which the
-- worker first becomes aware of the failure". (10): s 207B applies.
@ref ERA 1996 s 27BH(1)-(8), (10)
@export The last day to present a guaranteed-hours complaint to an employment tribunal under s 27BH of the Employment Rights Act 1996 as inserted by the Employment Rights Act 2025 (UK): the end of the six months beginning with the day after the trigger day (the end of the offer period, the offer, the notice, or the end of the initial information period), or for an information failure under s 27BF(2) beginning with the day the worker first becomes aware; extended for early conciliation by s 207B. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Complaint facts`  @desc The kind of complaint, its trigger day, and any early conciliation
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to present the complaint for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `early conciliation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN limit
    WHEN JUST e  THEN `the limit` limit `of a period from` start `extended by` e
    WHERE
        start MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `kind`
            WHEN `other information failure (27BG(8)(b))` THEN c's `trigger day`
            OTHERWISE Date (Day (c's `trigger day`) PLUS 1)
        limit MEANS `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` start
